{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "3b7e2f0c-8a4d-4c61-9e2b-5d1f6a9c0e47",
    "name": "PalmPesa API v2 (Async)",
    "description": "Request a mobile-money payment with the PalmPesa Payments API v2 and check its status.\n\nFull reference: https://documentation.palmpesa.co.tz\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Import this file into Postman.\n2. Open this collection's **Variables** tab and fill in:\n   - `api_token`: your API token from the PalmPesa dashboard.\n   - `payer_phone`: your own mobile-money number, for example `255712345678`. The prompt goes to this phone.\n   - `callback_url`: a public HTTPS URL on your server that receives PalmPesa callbacks.\n3. Send **Request payment**, approve the prompt on your phone, then send **Get payment status**.\n\nThese are real payments: each send of **Request payment** charges `amount` TZS to `payer_phone`\nand uses a new `transaction_id`. The collection sends `Authorization: Bearer {{api_token}}` on every\nrequest, and stops before sending if a variable it needs is still empty.\n\nKeep your token private: don't share or export the collection after adding it.\n\n## Statuses\n\n| Status | Final | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `INITIATING` | No | Accepted; the prompt has not been sent yet |\n| `PENDING` | No | Prompt sent; waiting for the customer |\n| `AMBIGUOUS` | No | PalmPesa is confirming the outcome; do not resend |\n| `COMPLETED` | Yes | Money received. The only status that means paid |\n| `CANCELLED` | Yes | The customer cancelled or did not approve |\n| `REJECTED` | Yes | The mobile-money network rejected the payment |\n| `INITIATION_FAILED` | Yes | The prompt could not be sent (see `failure_reason`); nothing charged |\n| `EXPIRED` | Yes | Not paid within about an hour (usually 45 to 60 minutes); no payment received |\n\nIn rare cases a late confirmation turns `EXPIRED` into `COMPLETED`, and `payment.completed` arrives\nafter `payment.expired`. Treat `COMPLETED` as paid whenever it arrives, and deduplicate callbacks on\n`event_id`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Request payment",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// A new transaction_id for every send, so each send is a new payment.",
              "// To repeat a request safely, use \"Request payment - identical retry\".",
              "var id = 'PM-' + Date.now() + '-' + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8).toUpperCase();",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('transaction_id', id);"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('202 Accepted', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(202); });",
              "var res = {};",
              "try { res = pm.response.json(); } catch (e) {}",
              "if (res && res.data && res.data.order_id) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('order_id', res.data.order_id);",
              "  console.log('Saved order_id ' + res.data.order_id + ' (status ' + res.data.status + ')');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v2/async/payments",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v2",
            "async",
            "payments"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"transaction_id\": \"{{transaction_id}}\",\n  \"amount\": {{amount}},\n  \"currency\": \"TZS\",\n  \"phone\": \"{{payer_phone}}\",\n  \"name\": \"{{payer_name}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{payer_email}}\",\n  \"callback_url\": \"{{callback_url}}\",\n  \"buyer_remarks\": \"Postman test payment\",\n  \"merchant_remarks\": \"Postman test\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "description": "`POST /api/v2/async/payments`\n\nSends a mobile-money prompt to `payer_phone` for `amount` TZS. PalmPesa answers **202 Accepted** with status `INITIATING` straight away and sends the prompt in the background.\n\n- The pre-request script sets a new `transaction_id` on every send.\n- The test script saves `data.order_id` for **Get payment status**.\n- `202` does not mean paid. Only `COMPLETED` does.\n\nLimit: 30 requests per minute."
      },
      "response": [
        {
          "name": "202 Accepted",
          "status": "Accepted",
          "code": 202,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            {
              "key": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ],
          "cookie": [],
          "body": "{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"message\": \"Payment accepted.\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"transaction_id\": \"ORDER-2026-000123\",\n    \"order_id\": \"PALMPESAV2A20261008120000123EFGH5678\",\n    \"status\": \"INITIATING\",\n    \"failure_reason\": null,\n    \"amount\": 1000,\n    \"currency\": \"TZS\",\n    \"reference\": null,\n    \"channel\": null,\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-10-08 12:00:00\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-08 12:00:00\",\n    \"status_url\": \"https://palmpesa.co.tz/api/v2/async/payments/PALMPESAV2A20261008120000123EFGH5678\"\n  }\n}"
        },
        {
          "name": "409 transaction_id used with different details",
          "status": "Conflict",
          "code": 409,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            {
              "key": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ],
          "cookie": [],
          "body": "{\n  \"message\": \"This transaction_id was already used with different payment details.\"\n}"
        },
        {
          "name": "422 Validation error",
          "status": "Unprocessable Content",
          "code": 422,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            {
              "key": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ],
          "cookie": [],
          "body": "{\n  \"message\": \"The callback URL must be a publicly reachable HTTPS URL.\",\n  \"errors\": {\n    \"callback_url\": [\n      \"The callback URL must be a publicly reachable HTTPS URL.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}"
        },
        {
          "name": "401 Missing token",
          "status": "Unauthorized",
          "code": 401,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            {
              "key": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ],
          "cookie": [],
          "body": "{\n  \"error\": \"Unauthorized\"\n}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Get payment status",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (!pm.variables.get('order_id')) {",
              "  throw new Error('Send \"Request payment\" first; it saves order_id.');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('200 OK', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
              "var d = {};",
              "try { d = pm.response.json().data || {}; } catch (e) {}",
              "var finalStatuses = [\"COMPLETED\", \"CANCELLED\", \"REJECTED\", \"INITIATION_FAILED\", \"EXPIRED\"];",
              "pm.test('status is a known payment status', function () {",
              "  pm.expect([\"INITIATING\", \"PENDING\", \"AMBIGUOUS\"].concat(finalStatuses)).to.include(d.status);",
              "});",
              "console.log(d.order_id + ': ' + d.status + (finalStatuses.indexOf(d.status) === -1",
              "  ? ' (not final yet; send again in a few seconds)'",
              "  : ' (final)'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v2/async/payments/{{order_id}}",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v2",
            "async",
            "payments",
            "{{order_id}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "`GET /api/v2/async/payments/{order_id}`\n\nReturns the payment's current status. Reads PalmPesa's records only, so it is cheap to call, but prefer callbacks and wait a few seconds between polls.\n\nOpen statuses: `INITIATING`, `PENDING`, `AMBIGUOUS`. Final: `COMPLETED`, `CANCELLED`, `REJECTED`, `INITIATION_FAILED`, `EXPIRED`. Only `COMPLETED` means paid.\n\nLimit: 120 requests per minute."
      },
      "response": [
        {
          "name": "200 Completed",
          "status": "OK",
          "code": 200,
          "_postman_previewlanguage": "json",
          "header": [
            {
              "key": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ],
          "cookie": [],
          "body": "{\n  \"success\": true,\n  \"data\": {\n    \"transaction_id\": \"ORDER-2026-000123\",\n    \"order_id\": \"PALMPESAV2A20261008120000123EFGH5678\",\n    \"status\": \"COMPLETED\",\n    \"failure_reason\": null,\n    \"amount\": 1000,\n    \"currency\": \"TZS\",\n    \"reference\": \"0289999288\",\n    \"channel\": \"TIGOPESATZ\",\n    \"created_at\": \"2026-10-08 12:00:00\",\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-10-08 12:01:30\",\n    \"status_url\": \"https://palmpesa.co.tz/api/v2/async/payments/PALMPESAV2A20261008120000123EFGH5678\"\n  }\n}"
        },
